# USJET — React + Vite (web). Not a native iOS/SwiftUI app.

## Product vision (four pillars)

1. **Warp Speed** — global `.aviation-pulse.aviation-pulse--warp` in `App.tsx` (fixed, z-index -1); keep page shells transparent.
2. **Stone wordmark** — `<UsjetWordmark>` + `.usjet-logo-stone` (chiseled Audiowide; `.AI` cyan gradient).
3. **Founder story** — three `IMG_0515` panels in `public/founder/`; grit copy in `Founder.tsx`.
4. **Liquid Glass** — web CSS mapping below (never SwiftUI in this repo).

## Liquid Glass (web mapping of iOS 26 concepts)

Use these CSS classes instead of SwiftUI `glassEffect` / `liquidGlassBackground`:

| SwiftUI / iOS 26              | This repo (React + CSS)                                      |
|-------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| `liquidGlassBackground()`     | `.liquid-glass-background`                                   |
| `glassEffect` + capsule       | `.glass-effect` + `.glass-effect--capsule`                   |
| `glassEffect` + rounded rect  | `.glass-effect` + `.glass-effect--rounded-rect`              |
| `GlassEffectContainer`        | `<GlassEffectContainer>` + `.glass-effect-container`         |
| `buttonStyle(.glass)`         | `.btn-glass` + `.glass-effect-interactive` on links/buttons  |
| `buttonStyle(.glassProminent)`| `.btn-glass-prominent`                                       |
| `.interactive()`              | `.glass-effect-interactive` — only on clickable elements     |
| `.tint()`                     | `.glass-tint-cyan` / `.glass-tint-blue`                      |

Modifier order (web): layout → visual glass classes → interactive classes → handlers.

Floating chrome: `AppNav` uses `liquid-glass-nav` + `GlassEffectContainer` (native-style capsule header).

Background motion: global `.aviation-pulse` in `App.tsx` (z-index: -1). Keep Hangar grid / page shells transparent so lines read through negative space.

Hangar workbench: `.hangar-tool-workbench` uses opaque glass for iframe clarity; do not make the whole page opaque.

## Founder page (web Liquid Glass — not SwiftUI)

- Page shell: keep `founder-page--warp` + `page-atmosphere` **transparent** so `.aviation-pulse` reads through.
- Intro hero: `<GlassEffectContainer>` + `.liquid-glass-background` + `.glass-effect` + `.glass-effect--rounded-rect` + `.glass-tint-cyan`.
- Story panels (vector fallback): same rounded glass on `.founder-story__visual-frame`; photo panels use `--photo` variant without extra blur over the image.
- Social links: `.btn-glass` + `.glass-effect-interactive` (interactive only on `<a>` targets).
- **Founder images:** place JPEGs in `public/founder/` as `IMG_0516.jpeg` (Origin), `IMG_0517.jpeg` (Fleet), `IMG_0518.jpeg` (Industry First), plus `usjet-hero-logo.png` for the hero.

Do not reference SwiftUI APIs in this codebase unless adding a separate native Xcode target.
